                <p class="text-slate-500">Before conducting in-depth visual analysis, this study first performed normality and significance tests on the data to ensure the business conclusions have solid statistical backing. <!--[cite: 2] --></p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
                <!-- Normality Test -->
                <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-slate-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
                    <h4 class="font-semibold text-lg text-brand-dark mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
                        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-brand-orange"></span> Normality Test (Shapiro-Wilk) <!--[cite: 2] -->
                    </h4>
                    <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-4">To verify the prerequisite assumptions for parametric testing, a distribution test was conducted on the difference scores of each participant. <!--[cite: 2] --></p>
                    <div class="bg-slate-50 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm">
                        <span class="block text-slate-500 mb-1">Result: p = 0.168 (> 0.05) <!--[cite: 2] --></span>
                        <strong class="text-brand-green">Conclusion: The difference data follows a normal distribution; the paired t-test is appropriate. <!--[cite: 2] --></strong>
                    </div>
                </div>
                
                <!-- T-Test -->
                <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-slate-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
                    <h4 class="font-semibold text-lg text-brand-dark mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
                        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-brand-green"></span> Paired-Samples T-Test <!--[cite: 2] -->
                    </h4>
                    <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-4">Compared the overall mean difference of all participants between Week 1 and Week 2, ruling out random error. <!--[cite: 2] --></p>
                    <div class="bg-slate-50 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm">
                        <span class="block text-slate-500 mb-1">Result: t(38) = 25.49, p < 0.001 <!--[cite: 2] --></span>
                        <strong class="text-brand-green">Conclusion: The increase in engagement scores between the two weeks is highly significant. <!--[cite: 2] --></strong>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
